# G9POS — Data Model Rules

## ID Convention
UUIDs only. Never auto-increment integers.
- Device-originated shop records: generate on the device
- Server-originated: `users.id` (`POST /v1/setup`, `POST /v1/users`); category/product/inventory-event ids from `POST /v1/catalog/import`
- `devices.id` is client-generated on first install

```dart
import 'package:uuid/uuid.dart';
final id = const Uuid().v4();
```
```go
import "github.com/google/uuid"
id := uuid.New().String()
```

## Sync columns — default, with exemptions
Default for device-originated business records:
```
id, created_at, updated_at, deleted_at, device_id
```
Exemptions (`DATA-MODEL.md` §1.2):
- `inventory_events` — no `updated_at` / `deleted_at` (append-only; SQLite-only `rejected_at` is not a soft delete)
- `sale_items`, `supplier_order_items` — nested payload children
- `users`, `devices`, `sync_queue` — not device-originated sync events

Filter `deletedAt.isNull()` only on tables that have `deleted_at`.

## Soft Delete — Always
```dart
// ✅ Correct — soft delete
Future<void> softDelete(String id) =>
  (update(table)..where((t) => t.id.equals(id)))
    .write(TableCompanion(
      deletedAt: Value(DateTime.now().millisecondsSinceEpoch)
    ));

// ❌ Wrong — never hard delete
await (delete(table)..where((t) => t.id.equals(id))).go();
```

## Users
Server-originated. No `USER_*` events.
- First owner: `POST /v1/setup` (empty table, atomic)
- Staff: `POST /v1/users` (at most one non-deleted staff)
- PostgreSQL-only: `username`, `password_hash`
- SQLite: `id`, `name`, `pin` (hash), `role`, timestamps — pulled so PIN unlock works
- Never pull or return `password_hash`

## Inventory Events — Append Only
- Never hard-delete rows
- Never store computed stock — always `SUM(quantity_delta)`
- `quantity_delta` is signed: negative = stock out, positive = stock in
- Grouped types (`INVENTORY_SOLD`, `INVENTORY_VOIDED`, `INVENTORY_RESTOCKED`): `reference_id` = parent sale or order
- Standalone types (`INVENTORY_ADJUSTED`, `INVENTORY_DAMAGED`, `INVENTORY_RETURNED`): `reference_id = NULL`

**The only permitted UPDATE** to an existing SQLite `inventory_events` row is setting `rejected_at` while `synced_at IS NULL` (G1).

**Local stock query (SQLite) — must exclude rejected events:**
```dart
final stock = await (selectOnly(inventoryEvents)
  ..addColumns([inventoryEvents.quantityDelta.sum()])
  ..where(inventoryEvents.productId.equals(productId))
  ..where(inventoryEvents.rejectedAt.isNull()))
  .getSingle();
```

**Server stock query (PostgreSQL) — no rejected_at:**
```sql
SELECT SUM(quantity_delta) FROM inventory_events WHERE product_id = $1;
```

## G1 — rejected_at (SQLite only)
`inventory_events.rejected_at INTEGER NULL`

**Invariant:** `rejected_at IS NOT NULL → synced_at IS NULL`
- Only set on rows the server never accepted
- Never sent to server, never replicated
- Enforced in the DAO **and** a SQLite CHECK constraint (not a Dart `assert`)
- Standalone: mark by event `id`; grouped: mark by `reference_id`

## SQLite vs PostgreSQL Differences
| Concern | SQLite (Drift) | PostgreSQL |
|---------|---------------|------------|
| Timestamps | INTEGER (Unix ms) | TIMESTAMPTZ |
| Booleans | INTEGER (0/1) | BOOLEAN |
| UUIDs | TEXT | UUID native |
| Extra columns | `synced_at`; `rejected_at` on inventory_events; `sales.server_received_at` (server-authored copy) | `server_received_at` on inventory_events (PostgreSQL only) and sales (authoritative); `username`/`password_hash` on users |
| sync_queue | Present | Not present |
| devices table | Not present | Present |

## Price and Currency
All prices stored as integers (Myanmar Kyat, no decimals).

## Timestamps
All timestamps are Unix milliseconds in SQLite.

## Migrations
- Never modify an existing migration file
- Every `up` migration has a `down` migration
- Format: `{sequence}_{description}.{direction}.sql`
- Migrations run automatically on server startup
